              run original and build from one state each: every register
              including R, all 48K RAM but the attribute cells the copy shows
              (checked against a clean copy, and that copy against the game's
              own restore, 9638 times) and 32 bytes of dead stack: IDENTICAL;
              9688 Layer 2 pictures, 4524667 pixels, against an independent
              model and the bitmap the copy wrote: IDENTICAL; 12 broken builds
              caught; 640 ABI cases, each hook entered at all 4 CPU speeds,
              both IFF values, 8 R phases; the start-up exact with and without
              NEXLOAD

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless: through the real .NEXCLASH loader on a
              private NextZXOS 26.11 card copy, default, each cheat and both,
              output byte for byte as nxc.py makes it, reaching play;
              15-minute soak against the original; flicker check; the overlay
              published outside the play rows

  Coverage    Scripted input, no human play: title, menu, the first rooms of
              all four commandos' zones, wipes between zones, deaths, game
              over and a new game; not reached: later rooms and zones, natural
